{
 "build": "kguilin",
 "note": "The k-guilin kit's adapter onto the material library (forked from biomes/guilin's) (core/materials/PLAN.md). The host's layers (47-host-land.js): ground.grass (the plain: ground.grass.lush, full colour, 1.5 m), ground.litter (the towers' feet), ground.sand (the wadi's bars and the lake's beach), ground.mud (the paddies, the wadi's channel, the pond's edge, the lake's bed), rock.wall (the towers: rock.limestone.karst, grey with black rain streaks and ochre iron stains), rock.blade (the stone forest's blades: the same stone greyed, keep 0, its grey from the vertex colour: Shilin's rock is grey, not Guilin's ochre), rock.top (a tower's cap under the scrub). The kit's slots (BIO.libSwap, 50-biome-kguilin-species.js): the karst cards Ys commissioned (card.jungle.clump.0 for the cliff scrub, card.vine.hanging.0 for the creepers: full colour), the broadleaf, orchard and pine cards (tinted grey, keep 0) and the barks. Cards of the library: rice (card.crop.rice: young, grown, ripe rows), the bamboo leaf (card.bamboo.giant), the stone orchid (card.orchid.dendrobium), silvergrass and its plumes (card.reed cells), ferns (card.fern.green), moss (card.moss), the lotus pad (card.lotus) and flower (card.lotus.bloom). Run python3 tools/textures/pack.py biomes/k-guilin after any change, then python3 build.py. The borrowed species (nwbay's prism gum, ironbark, fan-crown, cliff fig, flame-crown, crown fern, stilt pandan, lotus trumpet, pipe reed) take nwbay's own pack, read in place (build.py: matlib_pack.fragment(biomes/nwbay, 'nwbay')), so they look as they do in the bay.",
